   "daf": "147b",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "וְאֵין עוֹשִׂין אַפִּיקְטְוִיזִין בְּשַׁבָּת. אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: לֹא שָׁנוּ אֶלָּא בְּסַם, אֲבָל בַּיָּד — מוּתָּר. תַּנְיָא, רַבִּי נְחֶמְיָה אוֹמֵר: אַף בַּחוֹל אָסוּר מִפְּנֵי הֶפְסֵד אוֹכָלִין.",
   "en": "We also learned in the mishna that «one may not make a drug to induce vomiting» on Shabbat. «Rabba bar bar Ḥana said» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan said: They only taught» that this is prohibited «with a drug,» which is considered a medicine; «however,» inducing vomiting «by hand is permitted. It was taught» in a baraita that «Rabbi Neḥemya says: Even during the week,» if one need not vomit for medical reasons, «it is prohibited» to induce vomiting «because» it causes «loss of food.»"
  }
 ],
